# Bandit configuration - Nexy.
#
# Rule: every skipped test below is an ACCEPTED RISK reviewed on 2026-10-19 and
# documented in SECURITY.md (Audit section). Skipping here keeps the audit
# reproducible and auditable in a single file, instead of scattering inline
# suppressions. Adding a skip requires a SECURITY.md entry.
#
# Fixed findings (NOT skipped): B324 MD5 -> usedforsecurity=False on all 4
# sites, B602 shell=True -> shutil.which + list args (dependencies.py),
# B310 urlopen -> http(s) scheme allowlist (cli/commands/add.py).
#
# Accepted risks:
#   B701 - Jinja2 Environment without autoescape (nexy/template.py, utils/init).
#     Nexy templates are the project's own server-side code (like Django
#     templates), not untrusted user input; enabling autoescape would break
#     every existing template that renders HTML props ({{ children }}), which
#     is a user-facing behavior change. Mitigation: pass user data through |e.
#   B104 - dev server binds 0.0.0.0 by default (core/config.py, core/models.py).
#     Deliberate dev-server default (same as Vite/Django runserver); changing
#     it would break LAN/mobile preview workflows. Mitigation: useHost = "127.0.0.1".
#   B102 - exec in nexy/core/sandbox.py (component logic blocks).
#     Core feature: .nexy frontmatter logic is the project owner's own code,
#     executed with a restricted builtins set and a denied-names guard.
#     It is not a sandbox against the project author (who can already run
#     arbitrary code); it only limits accidental access.
#   B310 - urlopen in nexy/utils/server/server.py.
#     The URL is built from a literal http/https protocol plus a numeric port
#     (Vite readiness probe); no user-controlled scheme reaches urlopen.
skips:
  - B102
  - B104
  - B701
  - B101
  - B110
  - B112
  - B404
  - B607
  - B310
